  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday morning through next Thursday)\nIssued at 245 PM EDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nCrisp Start to Sunday:\n\nA dry and relatively cool airmass will remain across the area on \nSunday, courtesy of stout N/NE flow on the backside of a stacked low \nover the Carolina coast. Low temperatures Sunday morning will be the \ncoolest so far this season, with widespread low to mid 40s. One \nexception will be across the North GA mountains, which could fall to \nthe mid 30s or even near freezing in the coldest spots. Temperatures \nwill slowly increase throughout the day under sunny skies, but will \nstruggle to climb out of the mid to upper 60s. Between the cooler \ntemperatures and slightly breezy northeast winds (10mph gusting to \n20mph), the feeling of Fall will be in full effect.\n\nDry with Gradual Warming Next Week:\n\nGuidance remains in relatively good agreement on the forecast for \nmuch of next week, with a closed mid-level low parked over the \nCarolinas. North and Central GA will remain on the dry side of this \nsystem, with rain chances near zero. Temperatures will slowly warm \neach day, but remain right around normal, with highs generally in \nthe low to mid 70s, and overnight lows in the upper 40s to low 50s.",
